-- Where the water is on Sydney Harbour's 50 m height grid, cell by cell.
-- Architecture: Tom Dyer. Code and these words: Claude (Opus 5.5).
-- Heights: harbour_heights.words (NSW Spatial Services 5 m DEM via ELVIS, AHD71).
-- Rule: under 1.0 m is water; water spreads to a neighbour rising at most 0.45 m and under 3.45 m,
-- or rising at most 1.2 m while under 2.6 m (tile seams); the named places are land;
-- Tom Dyer's paint tom_paint.words wins over everything; pier shore ends and the Quay apron are land;
-- where the clean map tom_map_water.words sees a cell clearly, it decides (map aligned by Tom Dyer);
-- under a Power SLAM wharf or pier deck it is water; under the Opera House, CQ station
-- and towers it is land. W water, L land, X no height. Rows go north to south.

